  "notes": "Gare du Nord with its limestone south front, five principal glazed arches, clock, city figures, stone wings, iron-and-glass train sheds, platform furniture and open northern train throat. Roof slopes, masonry details, city figures and structural ironwork are visual reconstructions from ordinary photographs. The mapped footprint fixes the position and signed orientation. Platform slabs and column feet adapt to the coarse viewer elevations. The model retains the native rail paths, approach roads and surrounding buildings. The small annex volume follows its mapped plan with an approximate roof height. Below-ground concourses, signage schedules and working trains are outside the exterior scope. Physical-device timings are unmeasured.",
