    "placementHash": "sha256:ab921ac88b0a78bff1a79e84364d832731a1d814473c704c5035ffee7feec0a3",
    "notes": "The named Paris Gare du Nord PMTiles point and contiguous headhouse, shed and annex footprints establish the terminal associated with Q745942. The façade faces Rue de Dunkerque and the northern throat follows the mapped tracks. Roof slopes, masonry details, city figures and structural ironwork are visual reconstructions from ordinary photographs. The mapped footprint fixes the position and signed orientation. Platform slabs and column feet adapt to the coarse viewer elevations. The model retains the native rail paths, approach roads and surrounding buildings. The small annex volume follows its mapped plan with an approximate roof height. Below-ground concourses, signage schedules and working trains are outside the exterior scope. Physical-device timings are unmeasured."
  },
